{
    "background_story": "Rose was a free-spirited child who spent most of her summer days bouncing on the trampoline in her backyard. She loved the feeling of weightlessness and freedom that came with each jump. As she grew older, Rose's passion for trampolines only intensified. She began competing in trampoline sports, quickly rising through the ranks to become a national champion. But Rose's true joy was sharing her love of trampolines with others. She started a community program, setting up trampolines in local parks and teaching kids from underprivileged neighborhoods how to jump and play safely. Rose's infectious laughter and enthusiasm made her a beloved figure in the community, and her trampoline program brought joy to countless young lives.",
